    "title": "Event-driven order processing on AWS",
    "description": "Customers reach the storefront through CloudFront, which serves static assets and forwards API calls to API Gateway. Three Lambda functions handle orders, payments and reporting; order and payment data land in S3, while reporting queries run through Athena over the same bucket. Route53 provides DNS and the TLS certificate for the distribution. A CloudWatch alarm watches the Lambdas and, together with the order Lambda, sends notification emails through SES.",
